            <dl class="method-facts">
                <div><dt>What you measure</dt><dd>The loudness of each discharge at stops along the route. The maximum marks the fault.</dd></div>
                <div><dt>Typical pitfall</dt><dd>Listening while walking. Footsteps and traffic mask the thump: stand still for each shot.</dd></div>
                <div><dt>Instruments</dt><dd>
                  <ul class="station__products">
                    <li><a href="/products/ap-01-acoustic-pinpointer"><span class="station__model">AP-01</span> <span class="station__pname">Acoustic pinpointer, 80&ndash;1500 Hz, four filters</span></a></li>
                    <li><a href="/products/pg-32-surge-generator"><span class="station__model">PG-32</span> <span class="station__pname">fires automatically every 5 s</span></a></li>
                  </ul>
                </dd></div>
              </dl>
          </div>
        </li>

        <!-- STEP 4 -->
        <li class="method-step" id="step-4" aria-labelledby="step-4-title">
          <span class="method-step__node" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          <div class="method-step__head">
            <span class="method-step__num" aria-hidden="true">4</span>
            <h2 id="step-4-title"><span class="sr-only">Step 4: </span>Trace route: put the distance on the map</h2>
          </div>
          <div class="method-step__grid">
            <div class="method-step__text">
                <p>The TDR measures along the cable, not across the street. A cable that turns a corner can be 1,280&nbsp;m away along its length and well under 1,000&nbsp;m away in a straight line. Without the route, the pinpointer walks the wrong line.</p>
                <p>A transmitter puts an audio-frequency signal on the cable. A hand-held receiver picks up the magnetic field above it and follows the cable along the street, corner by corner. Pace the distance along the traced path, and allow for slack at joints and terminations.</p>
                <p>In practice you trace before you walk with the pinpointer. It comes last here because it turns a distance into an address.</p>
              </div>
            <figure class="method-step__fig">
              <div class="plate">
                <svg class="diagram dg-wide" viewBox="0 0 520 360" role="img" aria-labelledby="rt-title rt-desc">
